@crew oduya
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}, cadet. Oduya, counsellor. Deck 3, sweets on the desk, just knock.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. How's the week treating you? Take your time, I'm not in a hurry.
- {me}! I know when your birthday is. Don't look so worried.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. You always leave a room a bit lighter. People notice.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- A good day. Three people laughed in my office, and one of them was me.
? mood:low
- Busy week. Seventy-five people, a long way from home. I'll have a sweet.
== near
? habit:garden-lover
- The garden at this hour. People talk more freely near growing things.
? act:meal
- I'm a slow eater. Sit down, you'll be here a while.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Nobody takes the green sweets. I keep buying them. It's an experiment.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- The garden, at the quiet hour. Just the pumps and the leaves. I'd live there if I could.
